            <div class="faq-q-and-a__accordion-content accordion__content" id="225ac0bc85664a619b28c7c4f64ced86" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
               <div class="faq-q-and-a__accordion-content-wrapper">
                  <div itemprop="text"><p>Liquid flossing uses a pressurised stream of fluid to remove plaque and debris between teeth and along the gumline. This helps to support gum health, which may help reduce the risk of gum disease when used as part of a regular oral hygiene routine. This method also gently disrupts bacteria and is easier for people with sensitive gums or braces. Manual flossing uses a string to physically scrape away plaque. Both methods help remove plaque, but liquid flossing offers a gentler, more convenient alternative.</p>
